  "Question": "In the definition of an ellipse, what relationship holds between the distances from a moving point to the two foci?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Their sum equals a constant greater than the distance between the foci",
    "B": "Their difference equals a constant",
    "C": "Their product equals a constant",
    "D": "Their sum equals the distance between the foci"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "The sum is constant, and this constant must be greater than the distance between the two foci for the locus to be an ellipse.",
